---
import PageHero from "../PageHero.astro";

const contents = [
  { id: "about-this-notice", title: "About this notice" },
  { id: "information-we-collect", title: "Information we collect" },
  { id: "how-we-use-information", title: "How we use information" },
  { id: "services-we-use", title: "Services we use" },
  { id: "cookies-and-analytics", title: "Cookies and analytics" },
  { id: "international-processing", title: "International processing" },
  { id: "how-long-we-keep-information", title: "How long we keep information" },
  { id: "your-choices-and-rights", title: "Your choices and rights" },
  { id: "external-services-and-links", title: "External services and links" },
  { id: "children", title: "Children" },
  { id: "updates-to-this-notice", title: "Updates to this notice" },
  { id: "contact-us", title: "Contact us" },
];
---

<div class="page" id="page-privacy">
  <PageHero
    className="privacy-hero"
    title="Privacy Notice"
    lead="How 886 Studios handles information when you visit our website, subscribe, apply, or get in touch."
  >
    <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-12">October 12, 2026</time></p>
  </PageHero>

  <div class="section privacy-section">
    <nav class="privacy-contents" aria-label="Privacy notice contents">
      <div class="privacy-contents-desktop">
        <h2 class="privacy-contents-title">On this page</h2>
        <ul>
          {contents.map(({ id, title }) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{title}</a></li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <details class="privacy-contents-mobile">
        <summary>
          <span>On this page</span>
          <svg class="privacy-contents-chevron" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6" />
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <ul>
          {contents.map(({ id, title }) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{title}</a></li>)}
        </ul>
      </details>
    </nav>
    <article class="privacy-notice">
      <section aria-labelledby="about-this-notice">
        <h2 id="about-this-notice" tabindex="-1">About this notice</h2>
        <p>
          This notice applies to <a href="/">886studios.com</a>. 886 Studios is operated by
          Archelon Limited Company (the “Company”), a corporation organized and existing under the
          laws of Taiwan with its principal place of business at 13F-6, No. 205, Sec. 1, Dunhua S.
          Rd., Da’an Dist., Taipei City 106, Taiwan (R.O.C.). The Company collects and uses personal
          information as described in this notice.
        </p>
        <p>
          This notice does not replace separate privacy information that may be provided by
          services you choose to use, such as application, newsletter, or event platforms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="information-we-collect">
        <h2 id="information-we-collect" tabindex="-1">Information we collect</h2>
        <p>We may collect the following information:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Website information:</strong> pages viewed, interactions, referring pages,
            browser and device information, approximate location, and similar technical data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Application information:</strong> information you submit through our Tally
            application form, including contact, founder, team, and company information.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Newsletter information:</strong> your email address when you subscribe to
            ikigai Insights through Substack.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Communications:</strong> your contact details and the contents of messages you
            send to us.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell personal information.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="how-we-use-information">
        <h2 id="how-we-use-information" tabindex="-1">How we use information</h2>
        <p>We use information to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>operate, secure, maintain, and improve our website;</li>
          <li>understand website usage and the effectiveness of our programs and content;</li>
          <li>review applications and administer 886 Studios programs;</li>
          <li>send newsletters when you have chosen to subscribe;</li>
          <li>respond to questions and other communications; and</li>
          <li>meet legal, regulatory, and security obligations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Depending on the activity and applicable law, we rely on your consent, steps taken at
          your request, our legitimate interests in operating and improving our services, or our
          legal obligations.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="services-we-use">
        <h2 id="services-we-use" tabindex="-1">Services we use</h2>
        <p>We use service providers that may process information for the purposes described above:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Vercel</strong> for website hosting and web analytics;</li>
          <li><strong>Google</strong> for Google Analytics and website fonts;</li>
          <li><strong>Tally</strong> for program application forms;</li>
          <li><strong>Substack</strong> for newsletter subscriptions and delivery; and</li>
          <li><strong>Luma</strong> for event information and registration.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may also disclose information when required by law, to protect our rights or users,
          or as part of a corporate transaction. Their handling of information is governed by our
          arrangements with them and their applicable privacy notices.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="cookies-and-analytics">
        <h2 id="cookies-and-analytics" tabindex="-1">Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We use Google Analytics 4 to understand how visitors find and use our website and to
          improve our content and programs. This includes measuring page views and interactions
          such as clicks on application and event links and newsletter signup submissions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google Analytics uses first-party cookies and similar technologies to distinguish
          visitors and sessions. Information sent to Google may include cookie identifiers,
          pages visited, referring URLs, browser and device details, and website interactions.
          Google also receives your IP address, which can be used to determine your approximate
          location. Our custom interaction events record information such as the page, link
          destination, and button label; they do not include the contents of application forms
          or newsletter email fields.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google processes this information to provide analytics reports. For more information,
          read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites and apps that use its services</a>
          and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can restrict or delete cookies through your browser settings. Blocking some
          technologies may affect how certain website features operate. You can also install
          the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>
          in a supported browser to prevent Google Analytics from collecting information about
          your website visits in that browser. This does not disable other website analytics.
        </p>
        <p>
          Vercel Web Analytics provides aggregated website statistics without using third-party
          cookies. Your browser also connects to Google to retrieve font files.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="international-processing">
        <h2 id="international-processing" tabindex="-1">International processing</h2>
        <p>
          886 Studios is based in Taiwan, and our providers may process information in Taiwan, the
          United States, the European Economic Area, or other locations. Where required, we and our
          providers use contractual or other safeguards intended to protect information transferred
          internationally.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="how-long-we-keep-information">
        <h2 id="how-long-we-keep-information" tabindex="-1">How long we keep information</h2>
        <p>
          We retain information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which
          it was collected, including administering applications and programs, maintaining
          appropriate business records, resolving disputes, and meeting legal obligations.
          Newsletter information is retained until you unsubscribe or the subscription service is
          discontinued. Retention periods may also depend on settings and policies maintained by
          our service providers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="your-choices-and-rights">
        <h2 id="your-choices-and-rights" tabindex="-1">Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live, you may have rights to request access to, correction of, or
          deletion of your personal information; restrict or object to certain processing; request
          data portability; or withdraw consent. You can unsubscribe from newsletters using the
          link included in each email.
        </p>
        <p>
          If European data protection law applies, you may also lodge a complaint with the data
          protection authority where you live or work. Withdrawing consent does not affect
          processing that occurred before withdrawal.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="external-services-and-links">
        <h2 id="external-services-and-links" tabindex="-1">External services and links</h2>
        <p>
          Our website links to third-party websites and services. When you leave our website or
          submit information directly to another service, that provider's own privacy notice and
          terms apply.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="children">
        <h2 id="children" tabindex="-1">Children</h2>
        <p>
          Our website and programs are not directed to children under 16, and we do not knowingly
          collect personal information from children through this website.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="updates-to-this-notice">
        <h2 id="updates-to-this-notice" tabindex="-1">Updates to this notice</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this notice when our practices, services, or legal obligations change. The
          date at the top of this page shows when it was last updated.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="contact-us">
        <h2 id="contact-us" tabindex="-1">Contact us</h2>
        <p>
          For questions or requests concerning this notice or your personal information, email{" "}
          <a href="mailto:it@886studios.com">it@886studios.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</div>
